<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hand-trimmed fixture standing in for WindowsServer-2025-DC-1.1, PowerStig's first (and so far
  only) revision of the Windows Server 2025 STIG. Rule ids, field values and dscresourcemodule
  attributes are copied from the real processed data in the local PowerStig clone rather than
  invented, so this doubles as the field-shape survey #95's map asked for: every one of the
  eleven rule types WindowsServer-2025-DC carries gets a real rule here, trimmed the way the
  WindowsServer-2022-DC/-MS fixtures are (short Description, no VulnDiscussion/RawString prose).

  V-278090.a/.b is a real sub-rule pair sharing one registry Key, the same shape
  WindowsServer-2022-MS's V-103.a/.b exercises - .b additionally leaves its value to the
  organisation, so one pair covers both shapes at once. V-278134 is a domain-controller-only
  Kerberos policy with no WindowsServer-2022-MS equivalent (see the sibling MS fixture, which
  has no rule at this id), included so the survey also has an organisation-value AccountPolicy
  rule to check against 2022's shape.
-->
